    /*
       Narrow phones only: let the quantity stepper fill the row.

       Below 375px, buy-box-style.phtml pulls Add to Cart out onto its own line,
       which frees up the whole first row for the stepper and the heart. Without
       this the stepper keeps the compressed 34px/26px sizing set immediately
       above (meant for the three-in-a-row layout) and leaves a dead gap between
       itself and the heart.

       Deliberately placed here rather than in buy-box-style.phtml: the rules
       above use !important, and buy-box-style.phtml loads in <head> while this
       block is inline in <body>. Same specificity + same importance means
       document order decides, so anything overriding them has to live after
       them - i.e. here.

       375px is inside the 400px query above, so both apply and these win.
    */
    @media screen and (max-width: 375px) {
        /*
           The stepper's own wrapper is .shrink-0, so it needs an explicit grow
           to take up the freed space. The ID keeps this above that utility.

           Targeted by class, NOT by :first-child - quantity.phtml emits a
           <script> block before the stepper div, so the container's first child
           is that script element. :first-child matched it (structural selectors
           ignore display: none) and silently styled nothing, which is why the
           heart kept wrapping.

           flex-basis MUST be 0, not auto. With flex-wrap on, the browser decides
           line breaks from each item's hypothetical size - its basis - before any
           growing happens. On "auto" that basis is the stepper's content width,
           which is wide enough that the heart no longer fits beside it and wraps
           onto a line of its own. A basis of 0 means the stepper claims no space
           up front, so the heart always shares the row, and the stepper then
           grows into whatever is left.
        */
        #addToCartActions .ahy-qty-slot {
            flex: 1 1 0%;
            min-width: 0;
        }
        /*
           No width: 100% here. The pill is a plain block div inside the wrapper,
           so it already fills it - and a percentage width would feed back into
           the wrapper's content size, which is what pushed the heart onto its
           own row.
        */
        #addToCartActions .flex.items-center.border-2.rounded-full {
            justify-content: space-between;
        }
        /* Bigger tap targets, now that there is room for them. */
        #addToCartActions .flex.items-center.border-2.rounded-full button[type="button"] {
            width: 44px !important;
        }
        /* Takes whatever is left between the two buttons, keeping the number
           centred instead of pinned to a fixed 26px box. */
        #addToCartActions .flex.items-center.border-2.rounded-full input {
            flex: 1 1 auto;
            width: auto !important;
            min-width: 0;
        }
    }

